// Aury's Lighthouse (Aury_2; bible 4.7, 8.1, 8.6, 5.3; character-bibles.md §2, §8). Sable's brother, a cormorant,
// keeper of the faded third lighthouse. He does not know he faded. Act 2, by Sable's tether: the keystone is in his
// wings, and he recognises Wren (plant 5.3: "the Remnant in the third lighthouse recognising her"). Act 3: his island
// drifts to the Hollow and Sable sits with him, talking prices. She does not tell him. Wren can.
// Aury: asks whether you've eaten; does not know the difference; never "I'm dead".

title: Aury_Lighthouse
---
<<if has_flag("blank.aury.met")>>
    <<if has_flag("keystone.aury")>>
        Aury: Have you eaten? You look like you haven't. #still
    <<else>>
        Aury: Still humming, this thing. Take it, will you? It keeps me up.
        -> I'll take it.
            Aury: Good. Mind, it's heavy. The lamp won't miss it.
            <<flag keystone.aury 1>>
        -> Keep it. It's the lamp's.
            Aury: Suit yourself. It's company.
    <<endif>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Aury: A visitor! Up the causeway, in this. Have you eaten?
Aury: I keep the light. Sable rows out with the oil. Not lately. She's busy, I expect.
Aury: Have we met? You've a look. Like a chick I saw once, carried past, out of the white. #plant:5.3
-> Sable sent me.
    Aury: Did she! Tell her the oil's low. She'll know what that means.
    <<voice surveyor blank>>
-> Who carried the chick?
    Aury: A woman with a lantern. Walking fast. Didn't stop to eat. Nobody does.
    <<voice warden blank>>
-> ...
    Aury: Quiet. Like Sable. She talks prices so she doesn't have to talk.
    <<voice drift blank>>
Aury: Found this in the lamp's heart. Heavy. Hums. No use to a lamp. Take it, will you?
-> I'll take it.
    Aury: Good. Mind, it's heavy. The lamp won't miss it.
    <<flag keystone.aury 1>>
-> Keep it. It's the lamp's.
    Aury: Suit yourself. It's company.
<<flag blank.aury.met 1>>
===

title: Aury_Island
---
<<if not has_flag("act3.started")>>
    Aury: Have you eaten? The causeway's long. #still
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Aury: The island's moved. Or I have. Sable's coming, she says. Have you eaten?
<<flag blank.aury.island 1>>
===

title: Aury_Sable
---
<<if not has_flag("act3.started") or not has_flag("sable.tether_sold")>>
    Aury: Sable? Not lately. She's busy, I expect.
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("sable.aury_sat")>>
    <<if has_flag("blank.aury.knows")>>
        Aury: That's why the oil's late. Well. Have you eaten? #still
    <<else>>
        Sable: Oil's up. Rope's up. Sit down or row. #still
    <<endif>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Sable: Oil's up. Rope's up. Everything's up but you, Aury.
Aury: Ha. Have you eaten, Sable?
Sable: Don't. That's not a price. That's a favour.
-> Aury. You faded. Forty-one years ago.
    Aury: ...Oh.
    Aury: That's why the oil's late.
    Lighthouse: Sable says nothing. For the first time, nothing.
    Sable: Boat's leaving.
    <<flag sable.aury_told 1>>
    <<flag blank.aury.knows 1>>
    <<voice surveyor blank>>
-> The oil's on its way.
    Sable: It is. I'm rowing it.
    <<voice warden blank>>
-> ...
    Sable: Good. Sit. He likes company.
    <<voice drift blank>>
<<flag sable.aury_sat 1>>
===
